---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LeadForm from '../../components/LeadForm.astro';
import { STICKY_CONSULT } from '../../data/sticky-cta';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Gulf Property Investment Consultation: Cross-Market Shortlist"
  description="Compare Dubai, Abu Dhabi, RAK, Qatar, Saudi, Bahrain property in one consultation request. Independent research, licensed partner referral."
  stickyCta={STICKY_CONSULT}
>
  <section class="site-container py-12 md:py-16 max-w-3xl">
    <header class="mb-8">
      <span class="badge-pill mb-4">Cross-Gulf</span>
      <h1 class="mb-4">Gulf property investment consultation</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-[var(--color-muted)]">
        Not sure which emirate or country fits? Tell us budget, residency goal, and hold period, we route to the right market and partner.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5">
        <a href="#lead-form" class="btn-primary">Book my consultation</a>
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose mb-10">
      <p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> Gross yields run roughly 7 to 9% in Dubai, 6 to 8% in Abu Dhabi, Bahrain and Ras Al Khaimah, 4.5 to 7% in Qatar and 4 to 6% in Saudi designated zones. The right market depends on your residency goal and hold period, not on the highest headline number.</p>
      <p><a href="/compare/">Market-by-market comparisons</a> · <a href="/guides/gulf-residency-by-investment-guide/">Residency by investment</a> · <a href="/guides/best-gulf-country-property-investment/">Best Gulf country for you</a></p>
      <p>Hubs: <a href="/gcc-rental-yields/">GCC rental yields</a> · <a href="/uae-business-setup-property/">business setup to property</a> · <a href="/uae-expat-documents-property/">expat paperwork to property</a></p>

      <h2>What a consultation actually covers</h2>
      <p>
        The session is a research conversation, not a sales call. We work through four things in order: what the capital is for, how long it can stay committed, which markets genuinely fit that answer, and what the total cost of entry and exit looks like in each. Most enquiries narrow from five candidate markets to one or two within that hour.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where the honest answer is that a budget does not yet clear a threshold worth buying into, we say so. Invest Gulf takes no listing fees from developers, which is what makes that answer available to us.
      </p>

      <h2>What to have ready</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Budget range and whether financing is intended.</li>
        <li>Holding period, and whether the capital may be needed earlier.</li>
        <li>Objective: rental income, capital growth, residency, or personal use.</li>
        <li>Home country, since tax treatment and transfer mechanics both turn on it.</li>
        <li>Any market already under consideration, and why.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Markets we cover</h2>
      <p>
        Dubai, Abu Dhabi, Ras Al Khaimah and Sharjah in the UAE; Qatar, Saudi Arabia, Oman, Bahrain and Kuwait across the wider Gulf. Coverage depth follows where foreign ownership is actually workable, so the UAE and Qatar carry the most detail, with Saudi designated zones and Omani ITC areas treated as early-stage markets rather than as established ones.
      </p>
      <p>
        Background before the call: the <a href="/gcc-rental-yields/">GCC rental yields hub</a> for the comparison framework, and <a href="/guides/gulf-residency-by-investment-guide/">Gulf residency by investment</a> where a visa is part of the objective.
      </p>

    </div>
    <LeadForm title="Book a Gulf property consultation" subtitle="Dubai · AD · RAK · Qatar · Saudi · Bahrain" context="Gulf property consultation landing" />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
